Admin overview (Frontend, Backend, CI/CD, Cloud) 

Author: Samuel Mount
Date Updated: 4/22/26

This project has:

Frontend: Expo/React Native app (and web via Expo/React)
Backend: Node/Express API running in Docker on an EC2 instance
Database: Supabase Postgres (backend connects via DATABASE_URL)
CI/CD: GitHub Actions builds backend Docker image, pushes to ECR, deploys to EC2 via SSM
Edge: Nginx on EC2 (reverse proxy to backend container)
Key idea:

Code is built in GitHub Actions.
Artifacts are Docker images in Amazon ECR tagged by git commit SHA.
EC2 pulls the exact SHA tag and restarts the backend container.
Nginx routes internet traffic to the backend container on the server.

