Quick “where is stuff” map:

GitHub Actions workflow: .github/workflows/ci.yml
Backend Dockerfile: backend/Dockerfile
Backend server entry: backend/server.js
Backend runtime config helper (if present): backend/config/runtime.js
Frontend env/config: frontend/.env (local), plus frontend config files in frontend/
EC2 deploy script (on server): /opt/change-now/deploy-backend.sh
EC2 backend env file (on server): /opt/change-now/backend.env
Nginx config (on server): typically /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/... (exact name depends on setup)
ECR repo (AWS): change-now-backend in us-east-2
SSM: AWS Systems Manager “Fleet Manager” shows EC2 node online; deploy uses Run Command
Environments:

Local dev: run backend/frontend locally, talk to Supabase dev DB if configured
CI: runs lint/tests, builds image
Production: EC2 + Docker + Nginx; backend talks to Supabase using production DATABASE_URL
Security notes:

Do not commit production secrets. Production secrets live on EC2 (/opt/change-now/backend.env) or in a secret store.
If a secret appears in screenshots/chats/logs, rotate it (DB password, JWT secret).